        <title>Scoop</title>
        <link>https://Siborne.top/en/p/scoop/</link>
        <pubDate>Sun, 28 Dec 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
        
        <guid>https://Siborne.top/en/p/scoop/</guid>
        <description>&lt;img src="https://Siborne.top/p/scoop/bannerImage.png" alt="Featured image of post Scoop" /&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;why-use-scoop&#34;&gt;Why Use Scoop
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;scoop.sh&#34; &gt;Scoop official website&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On Windows, setting up a development environment has always been a complex and challenging problem. Without a unified standard, the installation methods for various development tools differ drastically, incurring a lot of unnecessary time costs. Scoop helps you install and manage common development software in a unified way, saving you the tedious steps of manually downloading installers and configuring environment variables.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For example, installing Python and Node.js only requires:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-powershell&#34; data-lang=&#34;powershell&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;scoop&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;install&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;python&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;scoop&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;install&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;nodejs&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;installing-scoop&#34;&gt;Installing Scoop
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Personally tested + official installation method&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Install the latest version of PowerShell from the Microsoft Store&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://Siborne.top/p/scoop/assets/image-20251204204702-qhzlv3b.png&#34;
	width=&#34;1920&#34;
	height=&#34;1080&#34;
	srcset=&#34;https://Siborne.top/p/scoop/assets/image-20251204204702-qhzlv3b_hu_5818130fdd011680.png 480w, https://Siborne.top/p/scoop/assets/image-20251204204702-qhzlv3b_hu_8523b4acd3edbb57.png 1024w&#34;
	loading=&#34;lazy&#34;
	
		alt=&#34;image&#34;
	
	
		class=&#34;gallery-image&#34; 
		data-flex-grow=&#34;177&#34;
		data-flex-basis=&#34;426px&#34;
	
&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Open PowerShell and enter the following commands&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-powershell&#34; data-lang=&#34;powershell&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nb&#34;&gt;Set-ExecutionPolicy&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;-ExecutionPolicy&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;RemoteSigned&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;-Scope&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;CurrentUser&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nb&#34;&gt;Invoke-RestMethod&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;-Uri&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;https&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;err&#34;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;//&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;py&#34;&gt;scoop&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;py&#34;&gt;sh&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nb&#34;&gt;Invoke-Expression&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you see the image below, the installation is successful&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://Siborne.top/p/scoop/assets/image-20251204205229-f18qg4o.png&#34;
	width=&#34;1241&#34;
	height=&#34;1078&#34;
	srcset=&#34;https://Siborne.top/p/scoop/assets/image-20251204205229-f18qg4o_hu_f49963283263e6eb.png 480w, https://Siborne.top/p/scoop/assets/image-20251204205229-f18qg4o_hu_e1fdc3aa93e6dd06.png 1024w&#34;
	loading=&#34;lazy&#34;
	
		alt=&#34;image&#34;
	
	
		class=&#34;gallery-image&#34; 
		data-flex-grow=&#34;115&#34;
		data-flex-basis=&#34;276px&#34;
	
&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scoop requires &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://aka.ms/wmf5download&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Windows PowerShell 5.1&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://aka.ms/powershell&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;PowerShell&lt;/a&gt; as its runtime. If you are using Windows 10 or above, Windows PowerShell is built into the system. However, the built-in Windows PowerShell on Windows 7 is too outdated, so you will need to manually install a newer version of PowerShell.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As many users set their Windows username in Chinese, the user directory also ends up with a Chinese name. If software is installed under the user directory using Scoop&amp;rsquo;s default settings, it may cause execution errors for some software. Therefore, it is recommended to install to a custom directory. For other installation methods, please refer to: &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/ScoopInstaller/Install&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;ScoopInstaller/Install&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;5
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;6
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-powershell&#34; data-lang=&#34;powershell&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;c&#34;&gt;# Set PowerShell execution policy&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nb&#34;&gt;Set-ExecutionPolicy&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;-ExecutionPolicy&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;RemoteSigned&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;-Scope&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;CurrentUser&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;c&#34;&gt;# Download install script&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nb&#34;&gt;irm &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;py&#34;&gt;scoop&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;py&#34;&gt;sh&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;-outfile&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;s1&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;install.ps1&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;c&#34;&gt;# Run installation, --ScoopDir parameter specifies the Scoop installation path&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;.\&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;install&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;py&#34;&gt;ps1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;-ScoopDir&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;s1&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;C:\Scoop&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;using-scoop&#34;&gt;Using Scoop
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Scoop&amp;rsquo;s official documentation is very beginner-friendly. Rather than repeating it here, we recommend reading the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/ScoopInstaller/Scoop&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;official documentation&lt;/a&gt; or the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/ScoopInstaller/Scoop/wiki/Quick-Start&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Quick Start guide&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4 id=&#34;common-commands&#34;&gt;Common Commands
&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;table&gt;
  &lt;thead&gt;
      &lt;tr&gt;
          &lt;th&gt;Command&lt;/th&gt;
          &lt;th style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;Purpose&lt;/th&gt;
      &lt;/tr&gt;
  &lt;/thead&gt;
  &lt;tbody&gt;
      &lt;tr&gt;
          &lt;td&gt;scoop bucket list&lt;/td&gt;
          &lt;td style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;List all buckets installed&lt;/td&gt;
      &lt;/tr&gt;
      &lt;tr&gt;
          &lt;td&gt;scoop search&lt;/td&gt;
          &lt;td style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;Search for software&lt;/td&gt;
      &lt;/tr&gt;
      &lt;tr&gt;
          &lt;td&gt;scoop install&lt;/td&gt;
          &lt;td style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;Install software&lt;/td&gt;
      &lt;/tr&gt;
      &lt;tr&gt;
          &lt;td&gt;scoop list&lt;/td&gt;
          &lt;td style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;View installed software&lt;/td&gt;
      &lt;/tr&gt;
      &lt;tr&gt;
          &lt;td&gt;scoop uninstall&lt;/td&gt;
          &lt;td style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;Uninstall software&lt;/td&gt;
      &lt;/tr&gt;
      &lt;tr&gt;
          &lt;td&gt;scoop bucket&lt;/td&gt;
          &lt;td style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;Manage buckets&lt;/td&gt;
      &lt;/tr&gt;
      &lt;tr&gt;
          &lt;td&gt;scoop update&lt;/td&gt;
          &lt;td style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;Update software&lt;/td&gt;
      &lt;/tr&gt;
      &lt;tr&gt;
          &lt;td&gt;scoop config proxy&lt;/td&gt;
          &lt;td style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;Set proxy for Scoop&lt;/td&gt;
      &lt;/tr&gt;
      &lt;tr&gt;
          &lt;td&gt;scoop reset&lt;/td&gt;
          &lt;td style=&#34;text-align: center&#34;&gt;Switch software versions&lt;/td&gt;
      &lt;/tr&gt;
  &lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;qa&#34;&gt;Q&amp;amp;A
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 id=&#34;can-scoop-be-configured-to-use-a-mirror-source&#34;&gt;Can Scoop be configured to use a mirror source?
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Scoop community only maintains installation configurations. All software is downloaded from the official download links provided by the software vendors, so mirror sources are not available. If your network environment causes repeated download failures, you may need a bit of &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://csdiy.wiki/%E5%BF%85%E5%AD%A6%E5%B7%A5%E5%85%B7/%E7%BF%BB%E5%A2%99/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;magic&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;why-cant-i-find-java-8&#34;&gt;Why can&amp;rsquo;t I find Java 8?
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;The reason is the same as above. The vendor no longer provides download links for Java 8. It is recommended to use &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/ScoopInstaller/Java/blob/master/bucket/ojdkbuild8.json&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;ojdkbuild8&lt;/a&gt; as an alternative.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;how-do-i-install-python-2&#34;&gt;How do I install Python 2?
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;For deprecated and discontinued software, the Scoop community removes it from &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/ScoopInstaller/Main&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;ScoopInstaller/Main&lt;/a&gt; and adds it to &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/ScoopInstaller/Versions&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;ScoopInstaller/Versions&lt;/a&gt;. If you need such software, you must manually add the bucket:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-powershell&#34; data-lang=&#34;powershell&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;scoop&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;bucket&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;add&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;versions&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;scoop&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;install&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;python27&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://google.com&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://www.google.com/images/branding/googlelogo/1x/googlelogo_light_color_272x92dp.png&#34;
	
	
	
	loading=&#34;lazy&#34;
	
		alt=&#34;Google&#34;
	
	
&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
        </item>
        
